{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected","id":768427,"title":"[2e/B&S] Diablerie \"stain\": how is it detected?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-18T05:19:16-08:00","id":768427,"title":"[2e/B&S] Diablerie \"stain\": how is it detected?","content":"So there are references to the stain of diablerie on a vampire's aura scattered throughout Blood &amp; Smoke, even a mention of how the aura of a vampire possessed by a strix has the same aura as a vampire who has committed Amaranth, and a merit that allows those who commit diablerie to avoid staining their aura (Plausible Deniability).<br /> <br /> ... Except under the B&amp;S rules there's no way for vampires to read each others' auras, as that discipline was removed from Auspex.<br /> <br /> Help me out? What am I missing here? Was this addressed in the 2nd edition version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T06:12:14-08:00","id":768450,"title":"","content":"Auspex manages it. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/32359-predatory-aura?p=32555#post32555\">I asked the same question</a>, the answer is in the next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:13:43-08:00","id":768515,"title":"","content":"Read Auspex 2, it's one of the questions you can ask. I like how this makes it easier to get away with it if no one has reason to check but there's still a chance someone will chance a question if they have one leftover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T02:46:36-08:00","id":769061,"title":"","content":"Aura's still exist. Vampires can still read them. The only thing 2e got rid of was that bloody chart with all the colours on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T06:43:00-08:00","id":769194,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the 2e Auspex 2 is almost functionally identical to 1e Auspex 2, it just lets the player say what they want to find out instead of the ST deciding what will be the most relevant, and gives the ST more freedom in how they describe the sensory input the player recieves rather than being bound to the chart of colors and their meanings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T07:48:31-08:00","id":769239,"title":"","content":"Resolute diablerist can get rid of diabolic stains by burning himself with fire, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:48:55-08:00","id":769288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=769239#post769239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resolute diablerist can get rid of diabolic stains by burning himself with fire, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this must be a Masquerade thing? Because I am pretty familiar with both editions of Requiem and I have never heard of this before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:54:58-08:00","id":769295,"title":"","content":"Diablerie gives you Tainted condition. Tainted condition resolves in (Blood Potency of victim) months. Each Aggravated Damage brings you one month closer to getting rid of it. It's in the Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> So a well informed, resolute diablerist with enough balls to fry himself a little with a lighter can erase all evidence of Amaranth in a single night. Which is probably why Amaranth is a great taboo; imagine how much more tempting it would be if this stuff was public knowledge. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T08:59:55-08:00","id":769302,"title":"","content":"You exchange temporary scars on your soul for permanent scars on your body.<br /> <br /> So, not <i>all</i> evidence of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:02:16-08:00","id":769306,"title":"","content":"Actually, it is not entirely clear whether Tainted and the aura stain are the same. The marks of Diablerie could last far beyond the Tainted Condition. Really, the only thing Tainted does is signify you have not fully &quot;digested&quot; the devoured soul yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T09:38:44-08:00","id":769341,"title":"","content":"Nothing in the Diablerie section or the Tainted Condition suggests it is the cause of the aura stain. And the example question listed under Auspex 2 is &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot;, not &quot;does this person have the Tainted Condition?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:29:47-08:00","id":774737,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the answers, everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2286-indarkestknight","name":"indarkestknight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:05:44-08:00","id":774805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=769341#post769341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in the Diablerie section or the Tainted Condition suggests it is the cause of the aura stain. And the example question listed under Auspex 2 is &quot;is this person a diablerist?&quot;, not &quot;does this person have the Tainted Condition?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, this is why it feels like Diablerie isn't worth it in VtR 2e. Do it just once and you're forever marked as having committed the greatest taboo/sin/crime.<br /> <br /> Also, I really wish the forum's editor didn't overwrite my browser's right-click menu with its own. That's how my spellcheck works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:24:51-08:00","id":774819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=774805#post774805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, this is why it feels like Diablerie isn't worth it in VtR 2e. Do it just once and you're forever marked as having committed the greatest taboo/sin/crime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I don't see it as significantly more dangerous than it was in 1e. Auspex 2 could still find it. Aura stains could fade in time, but the amount of time it took was longer than is usually covered in the course of play, in my experience so that only helped if you wanted it as part of your background. I've only seen three diablerist characters in actual play. One was an En. One was in a domain where Diablerie was permitted as a punishment for illegal Diablerie. And one was near the end of a long-running game and the player wanted her character to go out with a bang (which she did).<br /> <br /> Personally, I see it as something you always consult with the ST about. &quot;I'm considering playing a diablerist. How can we make this work within the game?&quot; And then together you can work out the details of who knows and is blackmailing you, who knows and you're coercing into keeping quiet, who has no idea, and what the consequences might be if they find out. It's not something you can do on a whim, but it's not something you <i>should</i> be able to do on a whim, in my opinion. Diablerie can be a chronicle-defining act, and as such I'm perfectly ok with the mechanics necessitating that a lot of groundwork be laid both in and out of character before doing it.<br /> <br /> And, of course, if you want to tip the risk/reward balance a bit more towards reward, it's easy to just rule that Auspex can only detect the Tainted Conditon. Just keep in mind that it will allow characters to literally burn the Diablerie stains out of their aura, which may or may not be a thing you want them to be able to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=774805#post774805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I really wish the forum's editor didn't overwrite my browser's right-click menu with its own. That's how my spellcheck works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I find that pretty annoying as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-26-2015, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T08:50:25-08:00","id":774839,"title":"","content":"It's really only worth it once you find more powerful vampires to commit diablerie on. It was incorporated in my last game and while I allowed one character to take a bane for diablerie, they still suffered the Humanity loss for related actions, like pre-meditated killing. At one point they had a whole gaggle of unprotected neonates to take advantage of and realized the benefits of sucking on newbies weren't really worth the quick slide down Humanity which led to them losing touchstones and becoming more likely to lose Humanity.<br /> <br /> And yeah you definitely want to know ahead of time if players are planning on doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T10:38:54-08:00","id":774903,"title":"","content":"I'd go with those answering &quot;Auspex&quot;, now it depends how you're playing this and if your question is really &quot;how to get away with diablerie ?&quot;. If you have a strict view about clan's disciplines in your chronicle, chances are only the Mekhet plus a couple of vampires will have the Auspex level to detect it. If it's the case, ask yourself a question: would the kindred as a whole give the power to the Mekhet to put a vampire to death ? They are telling is a diabolist, maybe it's true, maybe it's a ruse to put him down, you're the prince, you don't have the discipline: you don't know, what are you going to do ? And even if you do have the discipline, what if the Carthians starting to spread rumors about the prince calling political opponents diabolists ? This, and a lot of things in Vampire, is about politics. You have the good contacts, you prepared yourself for this, you have support, yes, you can get away with murder ; you don't, you're screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:01:40-08:00","id":774917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=774839#post774839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really only worth it once you find more powerful vampires to commit diablerie on. It was incorporated in my last game and while I allowed one character to take a bane for diablerie, they still suffered the Humanity loss for related actions, like pre-meditated killing. At one point they had a whole gaggle of unprotected neonates to take advantage of and realized the benefits of sucking on newbies weren't really worth the quick slide down Humanity which led to them losing touchstones and becoming more likely to lose Humanity.<br /> <br /> And yeah you definitely want to know ahead of time if players are planning on doing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What, no more discipline or skill dot for diablerizing another kindred? That can be plenty useful depending on specific target too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:07:14-08:00","id":774920,"title":"","content":"No, you get those, it's just better if you can get a Blood Potency alongside them. Especially when it comes to Skills, which cost the same as Humanity.<br /> <br /> Basically if you start losing Humanity, you have increased chance to lose more Humanity as you lose access to your Touchstones. And since losing all your Humanity means game over for a vampire, you're going to want to buy it back at certain points, especially since you become addicted to committing diablerie. You get low enough, your gain of a Skill point and a fraction of Blood Potency comes with a tax for Touchstones and Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-26-2015, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:27:59-08:00","id":774929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/768427-2e-b-s-diablerie-stain-how-is-it-detected?p=774903#post774903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would the kindred as a whole give the power to the Mekhet to put a vampire to death ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm now imagining Vampire Court using Dominate to force people to tell the truth instead of swearing on a Bible.<br /> <br /> &quot;Is Baron von Vampenstein a Diablerist? Answer truthfully!&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't think Dominate is an obvious power, so that lets the Ventrue and Mekhet work in cahoots, but it's still an added layer of security.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:32:36-08:00","id":774933,"title":"","content":"Yeah. One of the reasons I suggest you talk to your ST or players to see if they plan on committing diablerie is so you can, if you want, find reasons for the people who would find out about the act to take advantage of it, rather than just call for an executioner.<br /> <br /> In our case the sheriff was trying to usurp the Prince and wanted a loyal cadre that would really appreciate knowing where the hidden havens of elders are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}